1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:02,530
Everyone sleeps.
人人都要睡觉。

2
00:00:03,330 --> 00:00:06,260
Good sleep helps you get enough rest and stay energetic.
良好的睡眠能帮助你得到充分的休息，保持精力充沛。

3
00:00:07,060 --> 00:00:13,230
While you sleep, your brain processes the information it has received during the day and forms memories.
你睡觉时，大脑会处理白天接收到的信息，并形成记忆。

4
00:00:14,030 --> 00:00:21,590
Also, your body does lots of repair work—refreshing tired body parts, reducing pains and cleaning up waste in your body.
此外，身体还会做大量修复工作：让疲劳的身体部位恢复活力，减轻疼痛，并清除体内的废物。

5
00:00:22,390 --> 00:00:24,200
Today, people sleep through the night.
如今，人们一觉睡到天亮。

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:32,380
However, diaries, books and other records from the 15th to 17th centuries suggest people used to sleep differently.
然而，15至17世纪的日记、书籍和其他记录表明，人们过去的睡觉方式和现在不一样。

7
00:00:33,180 --> 00:00:37,730
People would go to sleep between 9 pm and 11 pm for a couple of hours.
那时，人们会在晚上9点到11点之间入睡，睡上两三个小时。

8
00:00:38,530 --> 00:00:44,340
They would wake up for a while, and during this period they might read a book, visit a neighbor or do some chores.
他们会醒上一阵子，这段时间里可能会读读书、去邻居家串串门，或者做些家务。

9
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:49,530
Afterwards, they would lie down for the second sleep, which lasted until morning.
之后，他们会再躺下睡第二觉，这一觉一直持续到早上。

10
00:00:50,330 --> 00:00:55,770
Researchers think it was the invention of the light bulb in 1879 that changed this.
研究人员认为，正是1879年电灯泡的发明改变了这种睡法。

11
00:00:56,570 --> 00:01:03,050
Electric lights meant people started staying up later, so when they finally went to bed, they slept until morning.
电灯让人们开始熬到更晚才睡，所以等他们终于上床睡觉时，就会一直睡到早上。

12
00:01:03,850 --> 00:01:07,280
The Industrial Revolution also changed how people slept.
工业革命也改变了人们的睡眠方式。

13
00:01:08,080 --> 00:01:13,830
Starting in the 18th century, people moved from the countryside to the city to work in the factories.
从18世纪开始，人们从乡村搬到城市，进工厂工作。

14
00:01:14,630 --> 00:01:17,200
People had to get up and start work at a certain time.
人们必须在特定的时间起床、开始工作。

15
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:23,760
To make sure people didn’t oversleep, knocker-uppers, also known as wake-up helpers, appeared.
为了确保人们不睡过头，出现了“敲窗人”，也叫“叫醒帮手”。

16
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:26,550
They made money by waking people up.
他们靠叫人起床挣钱。

17
00:01:27,350 --> 00:01:32,190
Every morning, they would walk down the street knocking on doors or windows with sticks.
每天早上，他们会沿着街道走，用棍子敲门或敲窗。

18
00:01:32,990 --> 00:01:39,260
As alarm clocks grew popular in the 1930s and 1940s, knocker-uppers weren’t needed any more.
随着闹钟在20世纪三四十年代流行起来，人们就不再需要敲窗人了。

19
00:01:40,060 --> 00:01:45,170
Today, our sleep is mainly influenced by both social pressure and electronic products.
如今，我们的睡眠主要受到社会压力和电子产品这两方面的影响。

20
00:01:45,970 --> 00:01:49,130
Falling asleep becomes hard and sleep quality goes down.
入睡变得困难，睡眠质量也下降了。

21
00:01:49,930 --> 00:01:52,990
Put screens away 30 to 60 minutes before bedtime.
睡前30到60分钟，把电子屏幕收起来。

22
00:01:53,790 --> 00:01:58,660
Keep a comfortable bedroom temperature, avoid bright light and reduce nearby noise.
让卧室保持舒适的温度，避开强光，并减少附近的噪音。

23
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:01,490
These will help you relax and wind down.
这些做法会帮助你放松，慢慢平静下来。

24
00:02:02,290 --> 00:02:08,120
If you have lots of thoughts or worries, writing them down before bedtime can help you put them aside for the night.
如果你有很多想法或烦恼，睡前把它们写下来，可以帮你当晚先把它们放到一边。
